{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions","id":1278657,"title":"Pantheons conflicts regions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-04T12:09:44-08:00","id":1278657,"title":"Pantheons conflicts regions","content":"Topic for pointing example World settings where two or more Pantheons are fighting over one region. What we have to this day:<br /> <br /> <b>Baltic Region \u2013 Aesir &amp; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278397-2e-bogovi-slavic-pantheon\">Bogi ( Bogovi )</a> &amp; Dievai (Baltic Pantheon) \u2013 Northern Poland, Latvia, Lithuania &amp; Western Russia</b> \u2013 Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a><br /> <br /> Slavic lands over Baltic Sea for centuries were raided by Vikings \u2013 and with them, by Aesir. Norseman brought their gods that fight with gods of Slavs. Now those relations are\u2026 tense. Both Aesir and Bogi know one another as best frenemies they can, at least with Titans danger in region.<br /> <br /> <b>Brazil \u2013 Brazilian Indian ( closest to Inuit ) &amp; Orisha &amp; Kami \u2013 Brazil </b>\u2013 Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3776_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3776\" data-vbnamecard=\"3776\">AutoDefenestrate</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a><br /> <br /> Brazil could be a very interesting place on a pantheon level. There may yet be a few of the native Gods around. Bahia on the other hand is called out in the book as having some vibrantly Afro-Brazilian versions of the Orisha. Meanwhile there are some huge enclaves of ethnically Japanese Brazilians, many either Buddhist or Shinto, in regions further north. I'm not sure that they would necessarily be against each other, but it's an interesting mix.<br /> <br /> <b>(Great) Britain </b><b>\u2013 Aesir, Theoi &amp; Welsh \u2013 </b>Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a><br /> <br /> The Aesir and the Welsh pantheons would have been in long conflict. The Theoi would have been brought in through the schools and high culture. Recently various peoples from the British empire of not so long ago brought in pantheons from many lands.<br /> <br /> <b>Southern Asia \u2013 Devas &amp; Yazata \u2013 India &amp; Pakistan</b> \u2013 Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a><br /> <b>Notice: </b>With social tensions between India and Pakistan thread carefully on this religious matters.<br /> <br /> Mithraism and a more Zoroastrian version of Manichaeanism expanded to India. Moreover some strands of Hinduism believe that Zoroastrian entities are gods in their own rival pantheon of Indian. So the conflict is not absurd since it is established that it is pre-Islamic and not that it came with the Muslims.<br /> <br /> <b>Tibet \u2013 B\u00f6n &amp; Palas ( the saints and devils of Buddhism ) &amp; Shen \u2013 Tibet \u2013</b> Proposed by \u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a><br /> <br /> The B\u00f6n deities conflicting with the Buddhist deities conflicting with the Shen. Traditional issues with the Mongols and Hindu Nepal for bonus stress.<br /> <br /> <b>USA </b><b><b>\u2013</b> Many, many Pantheons \u2013</b> Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a><br /> <br /> The USA as a whole would have to involved in some kind of a compact to allow pantheons to share space because they are the nation of nations. If the set up is tolerant in some areas were is it extra rigid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-27-2020, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T12:35:17-08:00","id":1278664,"title":"","content":"The Baltic Pantheon has no say in this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T12:46:31-08:00","id":1278666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278664#post1278664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Baltic Pantheon has no say in this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not know there was one, officially in setting. When looking like this - there is no place on Earth where some other Pantheon <i>will not be</i> intermingling anywhere. You can have Devas only from one worshiping emigrant in any place on World, don't we? I'm here wanted to point main, official Pantheons interactions in specific places to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-04-2019, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T12:50:38-08:00","id":1278669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278666#post1278666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did not know there was one, officially in setting. When looking like this - there is no place on Earth where some other Pantheon <i>will not be</i> intermingling anywhere. You can have Devas only from one worshiping emigrant in any place on World, don't we?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't know there was a Slavic Pantheon officially in-setting already. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We can have whatever Pantheons we want and make for ourselves, and I think when discussing issues like these, we'd do good to pay attention to the diversity rather than gloss over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T12:57:52-08:00","id":1278671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278669#post1278669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't know there was a Slavic Pantheon officially in-setting already. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Slavic Pantheon was in 1E <b>Companion</b> and is announced in <b>Scion 2E Demigod</b>. But you are right - I will point Baltic as third actor in opening post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T13:45:50-08:00","id":1278686,"title":"","content":"It seems to me more of a solution than a problem. It is easier to justify action from different pantheons in the same group of players.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T14:21:55-08:00","id":1278701,"title":"","content":"The Baltic pantheon (Dievai, I believe) are absolutely a thing. They haven't been acknowledged or addressed in any official capacity as of yet, and, I hate to be pessimistic here, but they probably won't be. That being said, all myths are true by itself confirms their existence, and I could see them being a very good candidate for a homebrew write-up. So it's definitely best not to ignore their presence.<br /> <br /> On the subject of territories with more than one claim to them, however, I have a question aimed at Watcher and Sacerdos, concerning their Zemis write-up. What kind of relationship do the Zemis have with the Loa? Also, unrelated to the topic at hand, but what are the Zemis' overall, collective, demeanor as a group? On a scale of Shiunesh to Abosom, are they more generally malicious or benevolent? I know very little about the Zemis, and I'm really curious about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T15:25:29-08:00","id":1278713,"title":"","content":"I don't think we see much in the way of published material on this kind of thing.<br /> Seriously just imagine the potential sh*storm over the Deva/Yazata conflict as a setting. Pakistan and India have a...unpleasant history and draging in deities into into (more so than in our world) is likely to upset a lot of people.<br /> <br /> Tying other such conflicts (such as the aforementioned Baltic Region) are marginally less 'dangerous' depending on the era (the further back, less blowback). So tread lightly.<br /> <br /> It should be fine if you A) know (and check with) your group, B) be careful with how things are presented and C) be smart about it.<br /> <br /> You probably already knew that, but things that go without saying have a tendency to bite some poor sod in the rear, so I said it.<br /> <br /> Now stupid question, which \u00c6sir/Bogi conflict in the Baltics did you have in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T18:33:04-08:00","id":1278740,"title":"","content":"Brazil could be a very interesting place on a pantheon level. It's not quite West enough to really touch any ancient Aztec lands, but one supposes that there may yet be a few of the native Gods around. Bahia on the other hand is called out in the book as having some vibrantly Afro-Brazilian versions of the Orixa. Meanwhile there are some huge enclaves of ethnically Japanese Brazilians, many either Buddhist or Shinto, in regions further north. I'm not sure that they would necessarily be against each other, but it's an interesting mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T20:53:42-08:00","id":1278757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278686#post1278686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me more of a solution than a problem. It is easier to justify action from different pantheons in the same group of players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's a reason I pointed it in the first place. With particular regions intermixing Pantheons we at least have reason for characters of two or more Pantheons in one area - AND characters can work as 'peace keeping group', trying to take the tension off from Gods factions. Story potential. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T21:02:36-08:00","id":1278759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278713#post1278713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we see much in the way of published material on this kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why we have fans topics on forum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278713#post1278713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously just imagine the potential sh*storm over the Deva/Yazata conflict as a setting. Pakistan and India have a...unpleasant history and draging in deities into into (more so than in our world) is likely to upset a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. ( Seen Doctor Who episode on India-Pakistan matter lately. ) <b>I'm just curious why Yazata are equated with Muslims in Southern Asia?</b> Muslims are Monoteists, right? There is nothing I see particulary Yazata about them. They can 'second-worship' any other Pantheon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278713#post1278713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now stupid question, which \u00c6sir/Bogi conflict in the Baltics did you have in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any, really. I just point good place for 'here we have history of Aesir / Bogi cultures interactions on large scale so Pantheons in area are logical to be here and interact with themselves'. It's more a Storyguide pointing 'when you look for using Aesir &amp; Bogi, look maybe into Baltic Region'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-05-2019, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T21:06:55-08:00","id":1278761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278740#post1278740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brazil could be a very interesting place on a pantheon level. (And rest of text )</div> </div> </div> </div>Sooo...<br /> <br /> <b>Brazil - Brazilian Indian ( closest to Inuit ) &amp; Orisha &amp; Kami</b><br /> <br /> You say then?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Fixed because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a> post from below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-05-2019, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T21:23:08-08:00","id":1278765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278761#post1278761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sooo...<br /> <br /> <b>Brazil - Teotel &amp; Orisha &amp; Kami</b><br /> <br /> You say then?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Our Indian Gods do not resemble any concept of the Teotel pantheon. They do not function as city gods with different names. They are more like the Inuit Gods if they pick up some pantheon that already exists in the game, without of course the whole thing about the cold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T21:31:36-08:00","id":1278766,"title":"","content":"And I believe that the Sebastianist sect should be represented in some way. They were relatively popular throughout the Northeast and had fans in Rio de Janeiro.<br /> <br /> They ruled entire cities and made sacrifices of human blood to remove the charm that prevented the true king from returning, and his people should be prepared with the misery, hardship, violence, oppression and death to receive the Kingdom (in the chosen city in that world) where all will be rich, beautiful, happy, healthy and will escape the fate of Oca Caetana (Death) and Ounce of Destiny and the Ounce of the Sert\u00e3o.<br /> <br /> In Pedra Bonita in Recife they killed 50 people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T21:41:46-08:00","id":1278767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278759#post1278759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can see that. ( Seen Doctor Who episode on India-Pakistan matter lately. ) <b>I'm just curious why Yazata are equated with Muslims in Southern Asia?</b> Muslims are Monoteists, right? There is nothing I see particulary Yazata about them. They can 'second-worship' any other Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not say they were. Please do not put words in my mouth.<br /> <br /> I am aware the Yazata are more closely associated with with Zoroastrianism, not Islam. I am also under the impression that thefewas conflict (complete with purges) between those two faiths in the past. Let's just not, ok?<br /> <br /> The Yazata are 'just' the closest pantheon geographical to the region that has a canonnical write up, with the historical conflict between them as the icing on the cake. Linking the very real life issues to such 'divine' baggage is something I'd like to avoid but I thought it would be a useful touchstone in regards to the can of worms being opened.<br /> <br /> Much like a game of set in the Crusades where G*d is helping both sides slaughter each other might be in poor taste if handled carelessly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T21:50:40-08:00","id":1278769,"title":"","content":"Mithraism and a more Zoroastrian version of Manichaeanism expanded to India. Moreover some strands of Hinduism believe that Zoroastrian entities are gods in their own rival pantheon of Indian. So I do not find the conflict to be absurd since it is established that it is pre-Islamic and not that it came with the Muslims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T01:39:51-08:00","id":1278787,"title":"","content":"Fixed because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a> post from below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278761#post1278761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Brazil - Brazilian Indian ( closest to Inuit ) &amp; Orisha &amp; Kami</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278765#post1278765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our Indian Gods do not resemble any concept of the Teotel pantheon. They do not function as city gods with different names. They are more like the Inuit Gods if they pick up some pantheon that already exists in the game, without of course the whole thing about the cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T02:44:10-08:00","id":1278798,"title":"","content":"New version of opening post, after collecting editing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions#post1278657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Topic for pointing example World settings where two or more Pantheons are fighting over one region. What we have to this day:<br /> <br /> <b>Baltic Region \u2013 Aesir &amp; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278397-2e-bogovi-slavic-pantheon\">Bogi ( Bogovi )</a> &amp; Dievai (Baltic Pantheon) \u2013 Northern Poland, Latvia, Lithuania &amp; Western Russia</b> \u2013 Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a><br /> <br /> Slavic lands over Baltic Sea for centuries were raided by Vikings \u2013 and with them, by Aesir. Norseman brought their gods that fight with gods of Slavs. Now those relations are\u2026 tense. Both Aesir and Bogi know one another as best frenemies they can, at least with Titans danger in region.<br /> <br /> <b>Brazil \u2013 Brazilian Indian ( closest to Inuit ) &amp; Orisha &amp; Kami \u2013 Brazil </b>\u2013 Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3776_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3776\" data-vbnamecard=\"3776\">AutoDefenestrate</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a><br /> <br /> Brazil could be a very interesting place on a pantheon level. There may yet be a few of the native Gods around. Bahia on the other hand is called out in the book as having some vibrantly Afro-Brazilian versions of the Orisha. Meanwhile there are some huge enclaves of ethnically Japanese Brazilians, many either Buddhist or Shinto, in regions further north. I'm not sure that they would necessarily be against each other, but it's an interesting mix.<br /> <br /> <b>Southern Asia \u2013 Devas &amp; Yazata \u2013 India &amp; Pakistan</b> \u2013 Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1624_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1624\" data-vbnamecard=\"1624\">FallenEco</a><br /> <b>Notice: </b>With social tensions between India and Pakistan thread carefully on this religious matters.<br /> <br /> Mithraism and a more Zoroastrian version of Manichaeanism expanded to India. Moreover some strands of Hinduism believe that Zoroastrian entities are gods in their own rival pantheon of Indian. So the conflict is not absurd since it is established that it is pre-Islamic and not that it came with the Muslims.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T10:40:50-08:00","id":1278835,"title":"","content":"The Caribbean also has overlapping pantheons, with the indigenous Taino Zemis and the later Loa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T11:40:23-08:00","id":1278842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278835#post1278835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caribbean also has overlapping pantheons, with the indigenous Taino Zemis and the later Loa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, kinda missed your earlier post. So, the Zem\u00ed have a very positive relationship with all of the coastal African pantheons that ended up losing people to the Atlantic Slave Trade. These enslaved people often ended up fleeing into the woods and there joining forces with indigenous rebels to fight against the Spanish colonisers together. You have to keep in mind, though, that the Zem\u00ed are incredibly bad shape, and thus don't have a lot of weight to throw around in an alliance these days. But they do try to take political stances, and thus have clear pro-African, pro-American, and anti-European stance in their &quot;international&quot; politics. The African pantheons we have so far, the Orisha and the Abosom, are actually both not that close with the Zem\u00ed - the Orisha because they only arrived after most of Ta\u00edno culture, and the Abosom because little of their lore was actually carried over into Jamaica. Their closest African allies are probably the Basimbi of the Kongo people, because that was the main source of slaves for the Spanish colonies while the Zem\u00ed were still more or less around. As for the Loa, I find it very hard to take <i>any</i> stance on them, seeing as they are a mixture of so many different elements. A lot of Ta\u00edno elements in there, in fact. I couldn't imagine writing them, and so I don't have a very clear idea of how they'd behave either, but I assume they share the general friendship between Zem\u00ed and African-descended pantheons.<br /> <br /> As for the relative niceness level of the Zem\u00ed, they are tough little cookies. They love their people and depend on them to survive, but they also believe in very strict ... uh ... parenting or something. If not worshipped enough, they will abandon their worshippers, support their enemies, or just hurricane them with extreme prejudice. They are not as horrible as the Shiunesh and not as sexy as the Theoi, some of them are downright friendly, but they also have their absolute psychopaths. So they are not exactly a cuddly pantheon. Also understandably prejudiced against White people, at least the way I'm writing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T16:43:14-08:00","id":1278892,"title":"","content":"Tibet, most likely, with the original gods conflicting with the Shen. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T02:40:50-08:00","id":1278936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278892#post1278892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tibet, most likely, with the original gods conflicting with the Shen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The B\u00f6n deities conflicting with the Buddhist deities conflicting with the Shen. Traditional issues with the Mongols and Hindu Nepal for bonus stress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T06:48:36-08:00","id":1278958,"title":"","content":"You could probably do an entire Dark Eras style series of historical settings based on this idea. The last days of Ptolomaic Egypt (Egyptian vs Roman vs Greek and maybe others), Camalot (Welsh vs Saxon plus Roman holdovers, Mithris, others), or the Mongol conquest of China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T06:55:57-08:00","id":1278961,"title":"","content":"Added to opening post... <br /> <b>Tibet \u2013 B\u00f6n &amp; Palas ( the saints and devils of Buddhism ) &amp; Shen \u2013 Tibet \u2013</b> Proposed by \u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10624_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10624\" data-vbnamecard=\"10624\">Sacerdos</a> <br /> <br /> The B\u00f6n deities conflicting with the Buddhist deities conflicting with the Shen. Traditional issues with the Mongols and Hindu Nepal for bonus stress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T19:42:39-08:00","id":1279103,"title":"","content":"Probably a minor one, but the American southwest of the greater Four Corners region - Utah, Colorado, New Mexico, Arizona. The various native nations have some long standing grievances with each other over assorted odds and ends which, while not as bad as they would've been 150 years ago, are probably still a sore spot for members of the Dine, Hopi, Ute and other pantheons. Added to this is the influence of Aztec mythology on aspects of Mexican immigrant pop culture, which might be another source of possible conflict, with various local gods thinking the Aztec gods are trying to horn in on their turf.<br /> <br /> Southern Florida might have something similar, with Seminole deities, the Santaria Orisha, African Orisha, Hatian Loa, Hindu gods, and others (say Apollo deciding to have some vested interest in South Beach's LGBT+ community or various moon gods hanging around Kennedy Space Center for nostalgia reasons) having to get along. Honestly that sounds like it'd make a great game setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-10T17:14:30-08:00","id":1280002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions#post1278657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Topic for pointing example World settings where two or more Pantheons are fighting over one region. What we have to this day:<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> <b>Brazil \u2013 Brazilian Indian ( closest to Inuit ) &amp; Orisha &amp; Kami \u2013 Brazil </b>\u2013 Proposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3776_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3776\" data-vbnamecard=\"3776\">AutoDefenestrate</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"641\" data-vbnamecard=\"641\">Ben Linus</a><br /> <br /> Brazil could be a very interesting place on a pantheon level. There may yet be a few of the native Gods around. Bahia on the other hand is called out in the book as having some vibrantly Afro-Brazilian versions of the Orisha. Meanwhile there are some huge enclaves of ethnically Japanese Brazilians, many either Buddhist or Shinto, in regions further north. I'm not sure that they would necessarily be against each other, but it's an interesting mix.<br /> <br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>As Brazilian of Japanese descendence, I must just correct a few notes. The biggest concentration of Japanese (and East Asians in general) are in the town of S\u00e3o Paulo (SP). Some neighborhoods of this same city are almost entirely composed by these people. Liberdade (Japanese, and more recently Chinese) and Bom Retiro (Korean) are good examples. There are many colonies of Japanese in the South of the country too (places like Santa Catarina and Rio Grande do Sul states).<br /> <br /> The African descendent people are actually in the entire country, but, as a place of cult, I would say Scion: Origin is right and Bahia in general has strong worship of African religions (it is in the North East of the country. The biggest state of that region). So, the Orish\u00e1s are strong in there, the Kami and Shen are more to the south.<br /> <br /> I would say the pantheon that most relies to the &quot;native Brazilian Pantheon&quot; (that would actually mean the &quot;Tupi-Guarani&quot; peoples. They would reach great part of the country, but places like Argentina and Uruguai as well) are more around the Manitou actually, with many exceptions...<br /> <br /> And that is it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23841-hayashi","name":"Hayashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23841_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T06:40:31-08:00","id":1280089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hayashi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1280002#post1280002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Brazilian of Japanese descendence, I must just correct a few notes. The biggest concentration of Japanese (and East Asians in general) are in the town of S\u00e3o Paulo (SP). Some neighborhoods of this same city are almost entirely composed by these people. Liberdade (Japanese, and more recently Chinese) and Bom Retiro (Korean) are good examples. There are many colonies of Japanese in the South of the country too (places like Santa Catarina and Rio Grande do Sul states).<br /> <br /> The African descendent people are actually in the entire country, but, as a place of cult, I would say Scion: Origin is right and Bahia in general has strong worship of African religions (it is in the North East of the country. The biggest state of that region). So, the Orish\u00e1s are strong in there, the Kami and Shen are more to the south.<br /> <br /> I would say the pantheon that most relies to the &quot;native Brazilian Pantheon&quot; (that would actually mean the &quot;Tupi-Guarani&quot; peoples. They would reach great part of the country, but places like Argentina and Uruguai as well) are more around the Manitou actually, with many exceptions...<br /> <br /> And that is it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're gonna specify to the Guaran\u00ed, we can stop with the comparisons and just say: the Anga, partially outlined here (though still in 1e format): <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/639477-the-anga-the-guarani-gods\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-guarani-gods</a> and possibly slated for God if I remember correctly. Though Brazil obviously has a huge number of other peoples, from the Ge, Arawakan, Carib, and multiple other language groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T07:38:10-08:00","id":1280104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1278936#post1278936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The B\u00f6n deities conflicting with the Buddhist deities conflicting with the Shen. Traditional issues with the Mongols and Hindu Nepal for bonus stress.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mongol gods, to my mind, treat these conflicts as 'oh you guys, you're adorable, I love you little scamps and I am going to kick the absolute shit out of you' - which is to say, the Mongolian faith has traditionally adopted a lot of ideas from their neighbors while retaining a group of extremely aggressive, ambitious gods, and to my mind that speaks to a kind of blithe arrogance in which the gods treat everyone around them like frenemies without actually thinking about how they are actually viewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T07:40:00-08:00","id":1280105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1280104#post1280104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Mongol gods, to my mind, treat these conflicts as 'oh you guys, you're adorable, I love you little scamps and I am going to kick the absolute shit out of you' - which is to say, the Mongolian faith has traditionally adopted a lot of ideas from their neighbors while retaining a group of extremely aggressive, ambitious gods, and to my mind that speaks to a kind of blithe arrogance in which the gods treat everyone around them like frenemies without actually thinking about how they are actually viewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Tibetan Buddhism a major factor in the disappearance of traditional Mongolian religious practices? It was like that for the Manchu, at least, and I thought I remembered reading something similar about Mongolia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T07:45:30-08:00","id":1280107,"title":"","content":"Yes and no. It was kind of a bloodless thing - the Mongols were absolutely fascinated by Tibetan Buddhism and a lot of it got integrated into their own beliefs. Basically it was a form of syncretism that ended up dropping a lot of the old-school Mongolian stuff over time, but which wouldn't, I think, have sparked a direct conflict between the two pantheons due to the way it happened unless the Mongol gods actually sat down and looked back at how it went and decided to blame the Bon for it - which some of them might, there are a few more introspective members who might do that, but it wouldn't really be a united conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T07:59:02-08:00","id":1280108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorsRattus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1280107#post1280107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. It was kind of a bloodless thing - the Mongols were absolutely fascinated by Tibetan Buddhism and a lot of it got integrated into their own beliefs. Basically it was a form of syncretism that ended up dropping a lot of the old-school Mongolian stuff over time, but which wouldn't, I think, have sparked a direct conflict between the two pantheons due to the way it happened unless the Mongol gods actually sat down and looked back at how it went and decided to blame the Bon for it - which some of them might, there are a few more introspective members who might do that, but it wouldn't really be a united conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why the B\u00f6n deities, though? They got just as fucked over by Tibetan Buddhism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-11T08:04:07-08:00","id":1280110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278657-pantheons-conflicts-regions?p=1280108#post1280108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why the B\u00f6n deities, though? They got just as fucked over by Tibetan Buddhism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me being dumb and confused because my coffee hasn't kicked in yet.<br /> <br /> Or I could argue that the Mongols tar with a broad brush anyway and will fight anyone, I guess, but nah it's just me being dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T09:47:12-07:00","id":1298351,"title":"","content":"Hey nice thread<br /> Northwest Brazilian here and i have thought a lot about creating a Brazilian setting for scion trying to reimagine how all the religious diversity would work on Scion<br /> <br /> In Brazil we had many waves of immigrants in the 19th and early 20th century, with the most remembered ones being the italian, germanic and niponic waves of immigrants you considered the Niponic one that was the last one but forgot the Italian and Germanic waves that happened during the reunification wars that IMO would totally bring the Theoi and Aesir for Brazil also we could consider 2 other immigrations waves that are less reminded the slavic and syrian-libanese immigration waves that IMO could be perfect to bring a small touch of the Bogovi and the Anunnas even if less present as the other pantheons<br /> <br /> But how they would interact with each other would be the most interesting,I'm planning a central conflict with the Theoi and the Orix\u00e1s in a cold war for a cultural hegemony with Kami and the Aesir as neutral players<br /> <br /> i think in the north and northwest the Orix\u00e1s would have total influence but their influence wouldn't only stay there but would spread for the whole country in varying degrees, specially in poor sectors of society but not limited to them, their presence is felt in multiple aspects, candidates make offerings in hope of winning elections, people in hardships go to Terreros expecting help for all sort of matters, offerings to Ex\u00fa, Xango, Yemanj\u00e1 and etc... can be very commonly found in multiple places. They would have a even more syncretic relation with the catholic church, the native gods would have a alliance with the Orix\u00e1s and the north would be their strongest seat of power, they are very protective toward his followers and aren't happy with the Theoi slowly encroaching and trying to take their place as strongest influence in the country.<br /> <br /> The Theoi are the second external pantheon to enter in Brazil and they are very influential, specially in the south, they came with the Italian immigrants seeking a better life and who were exploited by the coffee barons making Demeter, Hades and Persephone and their myths(especially the story of the kidnapping of persephone) far more important for Theoi faithful, since the reason they came to Brazil was searching a better and more prosperous lives therefore those gods and their stories would fit perfectly for them, with time the Theoi started to naturally spread their influence in Brazil specially on the field of arts and politics and the european inlfluence on Brazil and the appreciation of european culture by the Brazilian elites made it easier to spread to the high strata of population, their relation with the catholic church is generally good since both religions are very close for hundreds of years.<br /> The Theoi seeing themselves as the best and the most apt to rule with their self proclaimed superior culture seek to govern all other pantheons and establish a cultural hegemony.<br /> <br /> The Aesir and the Kami would be neutral in the conflict but for different reasons, The Aesir prefer to keep friendly relations with both sides because they see no use in backing one sided or be a third party on the conflict but have friendly relation with both is full of benefits not only avoiding unecessary bloodshed but Odin have access to 2 complete diffrent sources of Knowledge and he hopes allies in any conflicts with their &quot;titans&quot; but that isn't easy as he wanted to upkeep specially with Thor itching to test his might with Xango and Ogun, and Loki constantly trying to undermine that nautrality, The Kami are also neutral but for a complete opposite reason, they are neutral because of they are very isolationists, they keep themselves in their communites and avoid dealing with the major pantheon conflicts at least unti now...<br /> <br /> I don't think i'm capable to write about the Bogovi position because i don't know enought about them nor the Slavs who came here, I know lot about the Anunna which is my favorite pantheon but not enough about the Syrian-Libanese immigrants but since they are very urban for what i researched that would please the Anunna since they always praised urban life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","user":"Queer Snake","date":". 03-22-2019, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24396-queer-snake","name":"Queer Snake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T08:50:00-07:00","id":1415691,"title":"","content":"Britain would be an interesting case. The Aesir and the Welsh pantheons would have been in long conflict. The Theoi would have been brought in through the schools and high culture. Recently various peoples from the British empire of not so long ago brought in pantheons from many lands.<br /> <br /> The USA as a whole would have to involved in some kind or other of a compact to allow pantheons to share space because we are the nation of nations. If the set up is tolerant in some areas were is it extra rigid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc